
                Wien2Wannier Installation Instructions
                **************************************

This is wien2wannier 3.0, a modified version of wien2wannier 2.0.  It
was developed and tested with the WIEN2k version named in the file
`WIEN-VERSION' (WIEN2k 24.1).


What WIEN2k already contains
============================

WIEN2k ships wien2wannier 2.0: the programs `w2w', `w2wc', `wplot',
`wplotc' and `w2waddsp', the scripts `init_w2w', `write_inwf',
`write_win', `prepare_w2wdir', `wannier90_lapw' and others, and an `x'
script that knows `x w2w'.

Version 3.0 replaces two of these programs, `w2w' and `w2wc', and adds
two things WIEN2k does not have: the standalone program `w2w_hybrid'
and the driver `wien2wannier'.  It replaces no script of WIEN2k.  The
`x' script of WIEN2k 24.1 writes the def file that `w2w' 3.0 reads, so
this package carries no copy of `x_lapw'.  The other scripts
under `SRC' are those of wien2wannier 2.0; they are kept for reference
and are not installed.


1. Build
========

  $ cp make.sys.example make.sys       # edit: compiler, BLAS/LAPACK
  $ cd SRC_w2w
  $ make all                           # w2w (real) and w2wc (complex)
  $ make -f Makefile.hybrid            # w2w_hybrid (serial)
  $ make -f Makefile.hybrid acc        # w2w_hybrid_acc (OpenMP), optional
  $ cd ..

`Makefile.hybrid' links Apple Accelerate by default; on other systems
pass your library, for example

  $ make -f Makefile.hybrid LIBS="-lopenblas"

README has the notes for macOS.


2. Install
==========

The programs can stay where they were built.  The driver finds them
there (it looks beside itself, in `../SRC_w2w', in $WIENROOT and on
PATH), or is told with `--backend-dir'.  To have `x w2w' of WIEN2k run
version 3.0, put the two programs into WIEN2k, keeping the originals:

  $ cp $WIENROOT/w2w  $WIENROOT/w2w.orig
  $ cp $WIENROOT/w2wc $WIENROOT/w2wc.orig
  $ make install target-dir=$WIENROOT

`make install' copies `w2w', `w2wc', `w2w_hybrid' (and `w2w_hybrid_acc'
when it was built) and the driver `wien2wannier', and nothing else.
`make install-cli target-dir=DIR' installs only the driver.

The driver needs Python 3.10 or newer and no other package.


3. Check
========

  $ wien2wannier --version             # 3.0, and the programs it found
  $ wien2wannier --check --input /path/to/case --seed test --k-grid 8 8 8

`--check' validates an existing WIEN2k calculation and writes nothing.
`doc/hybrid/00-public-wien2wannier-cli.md' describes the driver and
`doc/hybrid/05-worked-example.md' a complete run.


4. Wannier90
============

Version 3.0 hands Wannier90 an isolated problem and needs no change to
it.  The results of the accompanying paper were obtained with the
Wannier90 development build ff955d1, which release 4.0.2 reproduces
bitwise.  With version 3.0 installed, `write_win' of WIEN2k prepares
`case.win' for Wannier90 and `wannier90_lapw' calls `wannier90.x', as
they do with version 2.0.

